-- Store registry for the live stock monitor (docs/research/09-retailer-registry.json,
-- surveyed 2026-10-01 with our honest user agent from a non-AU cloud IP).
--
-- * Stores with an open, robots-allowed Shopify / WooCommerce catalogue feed are
--   monitored by the generic adapters (enabled; the first scan is a silent baseline).
-- * Stores that served a bot challenge / 403, or have no feed, are recorded with
--   blocked_reason and stay member-sightings-only (adapter 'none'). The workers
--   re-try nothing on their own; an admin can re-probe from the Sydney server.
-- * Existing custom adapters (JB Hi-Fi's Algolia monitor, Target's category
--   monitor, BIG W / Kmart blocked adapters) keep their adapter; only metadata
--   is refreshed for them.

on conflict (slug) do update set
  name = excluded.name,
  kind = excluded.kind,
  state = coalesce(excluded.state, public.retailers.state),
  config = public.retailers.config || excluded.config,
  -- Keep hand-written adapters (JB Hi-Fi, Target, BIG W, Kmart) and their switch.
  platform = case when public.retailers.adapter in ('none', 'shopify', 'woocommerce') then excluded.platform else public.retailers.platform end,
  adapter = case when public.retailers.adapter in ('none', 'shopify', 'woocommerce') then excluded.adapter else public.retailers.adapter end,
  enabled = case when public.retailers.adapter in ('none', 'shopify', 'woocommerce') then excluded.enabled else public.retailers.enabled end,
  blocked_reason = case when public.retailers.adapter in ('none', 'shopify', 'woocommerce') then excluded.blocked_reason else public.retailers.blocked_reason end;
